flowchart TD
    IN[Application, rails, documents, cashflows]
    API{ML service endpoint}

    IN --> API
    API -->|POST /internal/agent| AGENT_ENTRY[Normalize rail fields and invoke Agentic graph]
    API -->|POST /score or /internal/score| DIRECT_SCORE[run_score directly]
    API -->|POST /explain| EXPLAIN_ONLY[Reconstruct explanation from supplied assessment]
    API -->|POST /stress-test| STRESS_SCENARIO[Adjust cashflows and run scenario score]

    subgraph GRAPH[Agentic LangGraph workflow]
        START((Start)) --> VALIDATE[Underwriting Orchestrator: validate schema, input, rails]
        VALIDATE --> ROUTE{Validation route}
        ROUTE -->|Invalid input| FAIL[Fail-Closed Handler: record reason and require review]
        ROUTE -->|No verified rails| POLICY
        ROUTE -->|Documents provided| DOCS[Document Intake Agent: extract supported bank statement rows; mark uploads]
        ROUTE -->|Verified rails, no documents| NORMALIZE
        DOCS --> NORMALIZE[Financial Data Analyst: normalize rows, quality checks, weekly series, features, reconciliation]
        NORMALIZE --> QUALITY{Data quality}
        QUALITY -->|Failed| FAIL
        QUALITY -->|Passed| AUTH[Authenticity Investigator]
        AUTH --> SCORE_A[Score authenticity from normalized features]
        SCORE_A -->|Scoring failure| FAIL
        SCORE_A --> AUTH_P[p_auth, model version, band and evidence flags]
        AUTH_P --> GATE{Authenticity gate}
        GATE -->|PASS| STRESS[Cash-Flow and Stress Analyst]
        GATE -->|Review or more evidence| POLICY[Deterministic Terms Policy]
        STRESS --> SCORE_B[Score cash-flow stress with selected variant]
        SCORE_B -->|Scoring failure| FAIL
        SCORE_B --> STRESS_P[p_stress and model version]
        STRESS_P --> CAPACITY[Calculate cautious capacity using p_stress]
        CAPACITY --> POLICY
        POLICY --> TRACE[Decision Trace Builder: reconstruct checks, predictions, policy, provenance]
        FAIL --> TRACE
        TRACE --> END((End))
    end

    AGENT_ENTRY --> START

    subgraph SCORING[Model scoring and decision policy]
        SCORE_A -->|local artifact available| AUTH_ART[ML Model A artifact: auth.joblib]
        SCORE_B -->|local artifact available| STRESS_ART[ML Model B artifact: stress.joblib]
        AUTH_ART --> AUTH_P
        STRESS_ART --> STRESS_P
        SCORE_A -. artifact unavailable .-> FALLBACK[Configured scoring service; labeled heuristic fallback if none]
        SCORE_B -. artifact unavailable .-> FALLBACK
        FALLBACK -. score result .-> AUTH_P
        FALLBACK -. score result .-> STRESS_P
    end

    TRACE --> SERVICE_POST[ML service continues after graph]
    SERVICE_POST --> MODEL_FEATS[Build model-specific Model A and Model B feature vectors]
    MODEL_FEATS --> MODEL_ARTIFACTS[Model-specific feature builders and trained artifacts: auth.joblib and stress.joblib]
    MODEL_ARTIFACTS --> MODEL_SCORE[Return p_auth, p_stress, versions or null on scoring error]
    MODEL_SCORE --> MODEL_MERGE[Prefer graph predictions when present; otherwise retain service predictions]
    TRACE --> MODEL_MERGE
    MODEL_MERGE --> UNDERWRITE[run_score: policy arithmetic still uses versioned heuristic underwriting policy]
    UNDERWRITE --> RESPONSE[API response: verdict, terms, model_scores, explanation, workflow_trace, decision_trace, agent_detail]
    API -. graph invocation exception .-> AGENT_FALLBACK[run_score fallback; mark agent_unavailable]
    AGENT_FALLBACK --> RESPONSE
    DIRECT_SCORE --> RESPONSE
    EXPLAIN_ONLY --> RESPONSE
    STRESS_SCENARIO --> RESPONSE

    subgraph OBS[Observability]
        TRACE_EVENTS[Decision steps and audit events]
        LANGSMITH[LangSmith: graph node runs and safe summarized tool spans]
    end
    VALIDATE -. audit .-> TRACE_EVENTS
    NORMALIZE -. audit .-> TRACE_EVENTS
    AUTH -. audit .-> TRACE_EVENTS
    STRESS -. audit .-> TRACE_EVENTS
    POLICY -. audit .-> TRACE_EVENTS
    TRACE -. emit traced run .-> LANGSMITH

    classDef warning fill:#fff0d6,stroke:#c07800,color:#382500;
    classDef output fill:#e4f5e9,stroke:#39834b,color:#173b20;
    class FALLBACK,AGENT_FALLBACK warning;
    class RESPONSE output;
